  <h1>How to Make Chicken Jerky</h1>

  <div class="answer-box">
    <p>To make chicken jerky, trim and slice lean chicken breast 1/4 inch thick, marinate 4–12 hours, then heat the strips to an internal temperature of <strong>165°F</strong> before drying at <strong>160°F for 4–6 hours</strong>. The 165°F pre-heat is essential — poultry carries a Salmonella risk that beef does not, and most dehydrators cannot reach a pathogen-killing temperature on their own.</p>
  </div>

  <ContentImage src="/images/chicken-jerky.webp" alt="Homemade chicken jerky strips on a dark board, dried and lightly glossy" eager={true} />

